         <div>
            <head>Poem encoding</head>

            <p>Use consistent encoding for structure, names, spelling, and textual features.</p>

            <list>
               <item>Use <gi>div</gi> with a stable <att>xml:id</att>.</item>
               <item>Encode headings in <gi>head</gi>.</item>
               <item>Use <gi>persName</gi> and <gi>placeName</gi> for entities.</item>
               <item>Use <gi>choice</gi> for original and regularised spelling.</item>
               <item>Mark supplied text with <gi>ex</gi> and deletions with <gi>del</gi>.</item>
               <item>Use <gi>unclear</gi> for damaged or uncertain readings.</item>
               <item>For overwritten text: use <gi>del</gi>
                  <gi>add</gi> inside <gi>subst</gi> Include place inside <gi>add</gi>as in example
                  below</item>
            </list>
            <p>See comments in this file for full examples.</p>
         </div>
         <!-- POEM ENCODING GUIDE

      div:
      xml:id should be unique and predictable.
      Example:
      <div type="poem" xml:id="rup_000001">

      head:
      Keep the title in <head>. Use <lb/> for line after Head
      Example:  <lb/>

      person name:
      Use ref to point to person in  persons.xml file
      Example: 
      <persName ref="../persons/persons.xml#P0001">R. Cole</persName>

      place:
      <placeName>Oxford</placeName>

      regularized spelling:
      <choice><orig>sceince</orig><reg>since</reg></choice>

      supplied from contractions, abbreviations:
      w<ex>i</ex>th

      deletions:
      <del rend="strikethrough">your</del>
      
      substitutions:
     <l n="6"><subst><del>Which</del><add place="above">Who</add></subst> each night          died,
  
      unclear:
      <unclear cert="medium" reason="damage">shoow</unclear>

     Rend values:
     Examples:
      <hi rend="italic">Pallace</hi>
      <l n="11" rend="indent">Goe strainger now if good thou art,</l>
         
         -->


         <div>
            <head>Date encoding</head>

            <p>Encode dates using <gi>date</gi> inside <gi>creation</gi>.</p>

            <list>
               <item>Use attributes for machine-readable dates (YYYY-MM-DD).</item>
               <item>Use element content for human-readable description.</item>
            </list>

            <p>See comments in this file for full examples.</p>
         </div>
         <!-- DATE ENCODING GUIDE

         Use attributes for machine-readable dates (ISO format: YYYY-MM-DD)
         Use element content for human-readable description
         
         EXAMPLES:
         
         Exact date:
         <date when="1622-04-19">19 April 1622</date>
         
         After a date:
         <date notBefore="1622-04-19">after 19 April 1622</date>
         
         Before a date:
         <date notAfter="1622-04-19">before 19 April 1622</date>
         
         Date range:
         <date notBefore="1622-01-01" notAfter="1622-12-31">1622</date>
         
         Approximate date:
         <date notBefore="1620" notAfter="1625">circa 1622</date>

-->
         <div>
            <head>pb to mark change of page or folio</head>
            <p>See comment in this section for instructions</p>

            <!-- Insert <pb/> at top of the page <pb n="..."/> AND at the point of transition (e.g. <pb n="9v"/>). 
           Images can be added later: Example, <pb n="9r" facs="../images/folger_va103_1/folger_va103_1_f09r.jpg"/>-->
         </div>

         <div>


            <head>Reference system for persons file</head>
            <p>Encode references using <gi>type</gi> inside <gi>ref</gi>.</p>

            <list>
               <item> for <gi>type</gi> use LOC plus URI for Library of Congress authority record
                     (<ref target="https://authorities.loc.gov/"/>)</item>
               <item>for <gi>type</gi> use ODNB plus URI for entry in the Dictionary of National
                  Biography (<ref target="https://www.oxforddnb.com/"/>)</item>
               <item>for <gi>type</gi> use AOx plus URI for entry in Alumni Oxonienses <bibl>Alumni
                     Oxonienses 1500-1714, ed. Joseph Foster (Oxford, 1891), British History Online,
                     </bibl>(<ref target="https://www.british-history.ac.uk/alumni-oxon/1500-1714"
                  />)</item>
               <item>for <gi>type</gi> use ACa plus URI for entry in Alumni Cantabrigienses
                     <bibl>Alumni Cantabrigienses: A Biographical List of All Known Students,
                     Graduates and Holders of Office at the University of Cambridge, from the
                     Earliest Times to 1900, ed. Venn, John, and John Archibald Venn (Cambridge:
                     Cambridge University Press, 2011) Print. Cambridge Library Collection (<ref
                        target="https://www.cambridge.org/core/publications/collections/cambridge-library-collection"
                     />) </bibl>
               </item>
               <item>for <gi>type</gi> use HPO plus URI for entry in the History of Parliament
                  Online (<ref target="https://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/"/>)</item>
               <item>for <gi>type</gi> use FAG plus URI for entry in the Find a Grave website (<ref
                     target="https://www.findagrave.com/ "/>)</item>
               <item>for <gi>type</gi> use TNA plus URI for entry for link to National Archives
                  record or will (<ref target="https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/"/>)</item>
               <!-- For example,  <ref target="https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/D882904"
                            >TNA, PROB 11/139/332: Will of Doctor Thomas Johnson, Doctor of Physic
                            and Medicine</ref>-->
               <item> for <gi>type</gi> use EMP followed by name of pdf file plus URI for website of
                  the Early Modern Practitioners Online
               <bibl>Early Modern Practitioners: The Medical World of Early Modern England, Wales
                  and Ireland, c.1500–1715, ed. by Jonathan Barry and Peter Elmer (University of
                  Exeter). Database (<ref
                     target="https://practitioners.exeter.ac.uk"/>).</bibl>
               </item>
              <item> for <gi>type</gi> use CCEd plus URI for Clergy of the
                  Church of England Database (<ref
                     target="https://theclergydatabase.org.uk/jsp/search/index.jsp"/>)</item>
            </list>

            <p>See comments in this file for full examples.</p>
            <!-- <ref type="LOC">https://lccn.loc.gov/n79103858</ref>
               <ref type="HPO">https://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1604-1629/member/fane-sir-george-1581-1640</ref>
               <ref type="DNB">https://doi.org/10.1093/ref:odnb/7197</ref> -->
         </div>
         <div>
            <head>Miscellaneious</head>
            <p>For insertaions above the line, etc. use <gi>place</gi> inside <gi>add</gi>
            </p>
            <p>Caret sign is ignored</p>
            <!-- Example: 
         <l n="11">There are such skilfull Doctors <add place="above">in’t</add> they say,</l> -->

         </div>




      </body>
